  "emphasis": {
    "primary": "Control by identity (Increase Damage Taken 35% on Ice Palace's circle; Decrease Damage Given 30% on Ice Coffin)",
    "secondary": "Burst offense, the broadest coverage and heaviest route (Damage on three Ice rows at 45/40/40; Increase Damage Given 35% on Frostbound Ascendancy)",
    "tertiary": "Self preservation (Decrease Damage Taken 35% and Heal 25 on Cryostorm Aegis)",
    "rationale": "Teno Yuki is an A-rank Genjutsu bloodline with the Control and Defensive traits, and its supported rows split the same way: two enemy debuffs on 60 AP attack casts (Ice Palace exposure, Ice Coffin suppression), three Ice Damage rows at 45/40/40 (Imperial Freeze, Ice Coffin, Ice Palace) under an Increase Damage Given passive of 25% + 0.15 per user level, a single 35% self damage buff on Frostbound Ascendancy, and the kit's only guard and heal on the 40 AP Cryostorm Aegis. Control is primary by trait identity, not by weight: exposure and suppression are single rows that make the Genjutsu kit a pressure tool, while Damage is the broadest tag (three rows) and its route gives the strongest row-weighted build (Burst 23 against 19 for Exposure and Bulwark and 18 for Suppression). The Aegis rows are the tertiary sustain route; stun, absorb and recoil are unsupported and untouched."
  },
